<body>
    <h1>Facial Recognition Training</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-m=
acro-tip">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-approve confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>This section is to contain any information about what is required for qu=
ality facial recognition training</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>Image Collection Guidelines for Facial Recognition Training</p>
<p></p>
<p>Overview</p>
<p></p>
<p>This document outlines the requirements and best practices for collectin=
g training images for facial recognition systems. Following these guideline=
s will help ensure optimal model performance and accuracy.</p>
<p></p>
<p>Minimum Requirements</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Quantity</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Minimum Images Per Person: 10 high-quality images</p></li>
<li>
<p>Recommended Images Per Person: 15-20 images for better model robustness<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Face Coverage: Face should occupy 60-70% of frame</p></li>
<li>
<p>Minimum Resolution: 224x224 pixels (higher is better)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Image Quality Specifications</p></li>
<li>
<p>File Format: JPG or PNG (uncompressed preferred)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Image Size: Minimum 1MB per image for adequate detail</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Face Positioning</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Primary angles: Front-facing and 3/4 profile views</p></li>
<li>
<p>Consistent eye line (looking at camera)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Natural head position (no extreme tilts)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Clear view of both eyes when possible</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Lighting Conditions</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Even, diffused lighting</p></li>
<li>
<p>No harsh shadows across face</p></li>
<li>
<p>Avoid backlit situations</p></li>
<li>
<p>Minimum 100 lux (bright enough to read comfortably)</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Image Clarity</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Sharp focus on facial features</p></li>
<li>
<p>No motion blur</p></li>
<li>
<p>No excessive digital noise</p></li>
<li>
<p>Clean lens and sensor</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Variety Requirements</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Lighting Variations</p></li>
<li>
<p>Indoor artificial lighting</p></li>
<li>
<p>Natural daylight</p></li>
<li>
<p>Overcast conditions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Side lighting</p></li>
<li>
<p>Front lighting</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Expression Variations</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Neutral expression (40% of images)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Natural smile (30% of images)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Other expressions (30% of images):</p></li>
<li>
<p>Serious</p></li>
<li>
<p>Laughing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Speaking</p></li>
<li>
<p>Professional demeanor</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Angle Variations</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Direct front face (40% of images)</p></li>
<li>
<p>3/4 left profile (20% of images)</p></li>
<li>
<p>3/4 right profile (20% of images)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Slight upward angle (10% of images)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Slight downward angle (10% of images)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Context Variations</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Different backgrounds</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Various clothing/accessories</p></li>
<li>
<p>Different times of day</p></li>
<li>
<p>Multiple locations</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>What to Avoid</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Blurry or out-of-focus images</p></li>
<li>
<p>Over or underexposed photos</p></li>
<li>
<p>Heavy digital compression artifacts</p></li>
<li>
<p>Resolution below 224x224 pixels</p></li>
<li>
<p>Excessive noise or grain</p></li>
<li>
<p>Composition Issues (nothing covering any part of the face)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Face occupying less than 50% of frame</p></li>
<li>
<p>Extreme angles (&gt;45 degrees from front)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Heavy shadows across face</p></li>
<li>
<p>Excessive glare or reflections</p></li>
<li>
<p>Multiple faces in close proximity</p></li>
<li>
<p>Sunglasses or protective eyewear</p></li>
<li>
<p>Face masks or coverings</p></li>
<li>
<p>Objects blocking facial features</p></li>
<li>
<p>Heavy makeup that alters face shape</p></li>
<li>
<p>Extreme facial expressions that distort features</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Best Practices for Image Collection</u></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Use a camera with minimum 12MP resolution</p></li>
<li>
<p>Clean lens before shooting</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use tripod or stabilization when possible</p></li>
<li>
<p>Avoid heavy post-processing or filters</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong><u>Before submitting images, verify:</u></strong></p>
<p>[ ] Minimum quantity met per person</p>
<p>[ ] Resolution requirements met</p>
<p>[ ] Proper variety across all categories</p>
<p>[ ] No technical issues present</p>
<p>[ ] Files properly named and organized</p>
<p>[ ] Backups created and stored</p>
<p>[ ] Model-specific requirements met</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong><u>Environment Setup</u></strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>Choose well-lit locations</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use neutral backgrounds when possible</p></li>
<li>
<p>Maintain consistent distance from subject</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure adequate space for proper framing</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p>Collection Process</p>
<p></p>
<p>Plan shoots across multiple days</p>
<p>Vary time of day for natural lighting differences</p>
<p>Mix indoor and outdoor locations</p>
<p>Document shooting conditions</p>
<p>Review images immediately for quality</p>
<p>Maintain backup copies of all images</p>
<p>Quality Control Checklist</p>
<p></p>
<p>Additional Considerations</p>
<p></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
